  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a user, I want to pick the look of the app in a gallery of themes — each shown with its colours, its name and its author, grouped by family — so that the app looks the way I like; and as a theme author, I want a theme to be a token file plus optional art, so that adding one needs no code.\n\nOperator request of 2026-10-28. M4 (operator 2026-11-07: themes, icons and appearance are all M4).\n\n### Scope\n\nThe contract is [`docs/THEMES.md`](https://github.com/ezzz/HFRnow/blob/dev-swift/docs/THEMES.md) §1–§3, §8.\n\n- **Engine.** Decode `App/SwiftHFR/Themes/<theme-id>/theme.json` (folder-synchronized, ADR 0012), resolve `light` / `dark` / `any` against the appearance LOT-121 already applies, expose the tokens through the SwiftUI environment and to the reader's CSS variables (the LOT-121/122 path: `--app-*`, #568's derived tokens). Store the theme id under a new `SettingKey` (`theme_id`, device scope unless ADR 0013 says otherwise); unknown id → Legacy. *(Adjusted at the claim, 2026-11-11: the file is `<theme-id>/<theme-id>.theme.json`, since the bundle flattens synchronized folders and two `theme.json` would collide; THEMES.md §3 updated in the PR.)*\n- **Legacy theme = today's app.** With Legacy selected every pixel is what LOT-121/122 draw now (hue slider, dark style, brightness, defaults unchanged). The other themes override tokens.\n- **Gallery** inside the existing « Thème » screen, below the shipped pickers: families (Classiques, Rétro, OG Web, then seasonal families from LOT-166 inside their window), a light + dark swatch (one swatch and « clair = sombre » for a single-variant theme), name, « par <auteur> », check mark; footer « Envie de proposer un thème ? Les règles sont dans le dépôt : docs/THEMES.md (voir le README). » *(Adjusted at the claim, per the operator note of 2026-11-11: built as one standalone view, `ThemeGallery`, which #420 (LOT-180) moves into its « Thème » sub-menu with light and dark previews; no second gallery. The hue slider, dark style and brightness show only while Legacy is the theme.)*\n- **One structure per appearance** (LOT-122 learnings): a theme change may rebuild the screens it wraps; an appearance flip rebuilds nothing; the shipped Standard path stays pixel-identical to no modifier.\n- **Contrast test**: every bundled `theme.json` decoded and checked against THEMES.md §3 ratios; a broken fixture theme makes it fail.\n- Consistency with #572 (one row, separator and state-tint definition), #646 (capsule text contrast) and #651 (MP title tones « in every theme », operator 2026-11-08): those definitions read tokens, they are not redefined per theme.\n\nNot here: the accent presets (LOT-180, #420), seasonal behaviour (LOT-166), the themes themselves beyond Legacy (LOT-192, LOT-193, Noël abusé in LOT-166, Samain LOT-191).\n\n### Legacy counterpart\n\n| SwiftHFR | Legacy @ 87fe0d1c |\n|---|---|\n| theme gallery | none (legacy has two themes, light and dark: `Classes/Constants.h` `Theme` enum; `HFRswift/Swift/AppSettingsView.swift:421-466` `themeSection`) |\n| Legacy theme tokens | `HFRswift/Swift/Common.swift:813-938` (`AppThemePalette`), `Classes/ThemeColors.m` |\n\nUX evolution: new GAP row (gap-new in the PR's `### Ledger`, id = this issue), class `b·operator` (operator 2026-10-28; defaults unchanged).\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-121 (#212, done), LOT-122 (#213, done), docs issue « THEMES.md / ICONS.md » (#?)\n\n### Model\n\nOpus 5.5 → Fable 5.1 (touches every screen and the reader; AGENTS.md §6).\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- none.\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] With Legacy selected, the `AppThemeTests` pixel comparisons of LOT-122 still pass unchanged (no regression on any screen).\n- [ ] A test theme (fixture) recolours a list, a pushed screen, a split column, a sheet and the reader; an appearance flip rebuilds no view below the modifier (counted `UIViewRepresentable`).\n- [ ] Contrast test fails on a broken fixture theme; passes on every bundled theme.\n- [ ] Theme id survives relaunch; unknown id reads as Legacy and is left in the store.\n- [ ] #651's read/unread MP title tones hold in every bundled theme (test).\n- [ ] View logic in `@Observable @MainActor` models tested with Swift Testing; each new test shown to fail without the change; `xcodebuild build test` green on iPhone 18 Pro and an iPad simulator (iOS 27.0); `App build + tests` CI green; UI strings in French; light, dark, Dynamic Type XL checked; no new dependency.\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, docs/THEMES.md, App/README.md, ADR 0012, ADR 0013, LOT-121 and LOT-122 specs, #572. Claim with `/claim <session-id>`; PR body `LOT-188`, `Closes #<this issue>`, `Claim: <session-id>`; spec `docs/lots/LOT-188-theme-engine.md` from the TEMPLATE.",
