   "updated_at": "2026-11-11T21:40:36Z",
   "body": "**Operator decision requested (LOT-188, PR #829).** The scope bullet says #572/#651 definitions « read tokens ». In #829, native list rows, separators, selection and native text keep the **system** colours of the appearance a theme shows in. A theme recolours:\n- the tint (`accentText`);\n- prominent buttons (`accent`/`onAccent`);\n- every themed screen background;\n- the unread capsule;\n- the whole reader.\n\nRecolouring rows means a per-row `listRowBackground` on every list. Options:\n- **(a)** accept this scope for LOT-188, with native rows and text as a follow-up issue if wanted (LOT-192's Rétro 5250 will need it);\n- **(b)** extend #829 to every list now (much larger PR, more macOS runs).\n\nThe PR is written for (a); the spec says so under \"What a theme does not change\".\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
